Raw stdio transcript between client c1 and the codedev-study-plan server (--> client to server, <-- server to client):

--> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"initialize","params":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{},"clientInfo":{"name":"codedev-study-plan-web","version":"1.4.0"}}}
<-- {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{"tools":{"listChanged":false}},"serverInfo":{"name":"codedev-study-plan","version":"0.9.2"}}}
--> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"notifications/initialized"}
--> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"method":"tools/list"}

Statement: "The server must not send any reply to the third message, not even an error, because the message has no id."

The model asked for lesson search during run_b207. Transcript:

--> {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":14,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"search_lessons","arguments":{"query":"SQL joins","limit":3}}}
<-- {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":14,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Lesson search is unavailable (timeout after 3 s). Try again or plan without search."}],"isError":true}}

Statement: "This is a tool execution error rather than a protocol error: the request reached search_lessons, and the text is meant to be passed back to the model so it can decide what to do next."
